Historical qualification: This is a religious narrative, not a historically verifiable account of the origin of the tenfold group. Its importance lies in the theological meaning later traditions draw from it and in the textual contexts in which it appears.
5. Are there always exactly ten Mahāvidyās?
Ten is the best-known and most widely recognized grouping, but the broader use of mahāvidyā in Tantric literature is not always restricted to ten Goddesses.

Some textual traditions contain different lists or use the term more broadly. David Kinsley's study notes that both the membership and order of the tenfold group vary among sources. 
