Identity and theological significance
Mātaṅgī is associated with speech, music, learning, artistic expression, and knowledge. In several forms, her imagery has affinities with Sarasvatī, the Goddess widely associated with learning and the arts.

Yet Mātaṅgī is not simply another name for Sarasvatī. Her place within the Mahāvidyā group gives her a distinct Tantric identity.

Some Mātaṅgī traditions also engage with questions of purity, social boundaries, and forms of knowledge that conventional social categories marginalize. These features make her particularly interesting in comparative studies of religion and society.
